<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Order of the Golden Fleece</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1430">1430</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Order of the Golden Fleece is a chivalric order founded in 1430 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-the-good">Philip the Good</a>, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>, at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bruges">Bruges</a>. It bound the leading nobles of the Burgundian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> to the duke. It passed with the Burgundian inheritance to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>, whose Spanish and Austrian branches both continued it; knights included the Counts of Egmont and Horne.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/order-of-the-golden-fleece.jpg" alt="Order of the Golden Fleece" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexeinikolayevichromanov · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Order_of_the_Golden_Fleece_AEA_Collections.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
